falx.en:
n. A curved fold or process of the dura mater or the peritoneum;
   esp., one of the partitionlike folds of the dura mater which extend
   into the great fissures of the brain.

fangle.en:
v. t. Something new-fashioned; a foolish innovation; a gewgaw;
   a trifling ornament.
v. t. To fashion.

fearnaught.en:
n. A fearless person.
n. A stout woolen cloth of great thickness; dreadnaught;
   also, a warm garment.

filthiness.en:
n. The state of being filthy.
n. That which is filthy, or makes filthy; foulness;
   nastiness; corruption; pollution; impurity.

flagrancy.en:
n. A burning; great heat; inflammation.
n. The condition or quality of being flagrant; atrocity;
   heiniousness; enormity; excess.

foppery.en:
n. The behavior, dress, or other indication of a fop;
   coxcombry; affectation of show; showy folly.
n. Folly; foolery.

